  "prefLabel": "Env-Wq 1802.09 Mouth",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Wq 1802.09 “Mouth” means, for a tidal river, the lower end of the river where a line that forms a right angle with at least one bank of the river can be drawn across the river channel from bank to bank.\n\nSource. #9657, eff 2-22-10; ss by #12185, eff 5-25-17",
